{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536769-why-the-hell-is-the-grondr-one-of-the-lost-breeds","id":1536769,"title":"Why the Hell is the Grondr one of the lost breeds?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-06-03T17:08:26-07:00","id":1536769,"title":"Why the Hell is the Grondr one of the lost breeds?","content":"I can get the other two being lost, The werebats being unable to make more due to there Patron spirit being captured, and the Apis lost there main Wildkin, the Auroch(even thought it spreads all the way to India, and there are a lot of wild bovine species that they can use)<br /> <br /> But the Grondr are Wereboars, where even if we narrows that down to the Eurasia Boar, it has a range that IS FUCKING MASSIVE<br /> <br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img alt=\"The range of the Eurasia Boar, which is apoly named\" width=\"1080\" height=\"613\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.redd.it/vwv1v9i28u671.jpg\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.redd.it/vwv1v9i28u671.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.redd.it/vwv1v9i28u671.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> <br /> JUST LOOK AT IT!<br /> <br /> another point I see is that the Kinfolk of the Grondr domesticed there KinBoars<br /> <br /> <br /> If that is the case, why hasn't something similar happened to the Other changing breeds, plus if the red Talons exist for the Goruo, it is not a far Fetched that the Grondr could have another thing like them.<br /> <br /> Second of all, do you see the Massive land Area, how the hell are you going to Organize a Genocide,and make sure it sticks.<br /> <br /> Do people realize just how hard a genocide is, for fucks sake a shit tons of groups of people have been driven though Mud and have come out on top.<br /> And hunting down WildKin, and finding settlements is not easy in a Pre Bronze Age Europe. Do people realize just how hard it is to Kill a boar, and how tough they are?<br /> Plus trying to kill a Herd of Kin might trigger the first change in one of them, which would just be MESSY even with a prephared pack.<br /> <br /> <br /> So it's either someone gives me a good explation on why they are all dead, or I willl...<br /> <br /> Well this the computer so I cant do much.<br /> <br /> uh...<br /> be angery I guess?<br /> Could write a<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T17:29:28-07:00","id":1536772,"title":"","content":"Just having kin somewhere in the world doesn't mean your Breed is still viable. If their members, patrons and culture were murdered to such an extent that their identity was broken, there would simply be more true born Grondr. Unless Gaia wanted to do something about it or the Garou did some work to fix the things they broke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T21:11:13-07:00","id":1536781,"title":"","content":"That's Skull Pig territory now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T23:01:06-07:00","id":1536833,"title":"","content":"The Changing Breeds should reflect the actual real world legends of what animals that people turn into. And these tend to be actual predator animals. I don't think there are actual folklore or legends of people turning into Boars. So wereboars should not be thing in a Gothic horror world. That's more of a fantasy thing. The lost Breeds of Grondr, Apis, and Cazamotz make sense as breeds that don't survive as we do not have legends of them.<br /> <br /> I do realize that canon does have examples of such creatures. By folklore or mythological standards, there shouldn't be Ananasi, Corax, or Ratkin either. So my pleas, while logical, aren't supported by the canon. But I would argue those are mistakes in the setting. The developers allowed their gothic horror setting to become a fantasy setting, which was a mistake.<br /> <br /> Just my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-06T01:02:57-07:00","id":1536861,"title":"","content":"Hm, is the world of Werewolf a Gothic Horror setting, though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-06T03:39:41-07:00","id":1536862,"title":"","content":"You could always homebrew it so that the Grondr didn\u2019t die in the War of Rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-06T04:32:11-07:00","id":1536864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536769-why-the-hell-is-the-grondr-one-of-the-lost-breeds?p=1536833#post1536833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Changing Breeds should reflect the actual real world legends of what animals that people turn into. And these tend to be actual predator animals. I don't think there are actual folklore or legends of people turning into Boars. So wereboars should not be thing in a Gothic horror world. That's more of a fantasy thing. The lost Breeds of Grondr, Apis, and Cazamotz make sense as breeds that don't survive as we do not have legends of them.<br /> <br /> I do realize that canon does have examples of such creatures. By folklore or mythological standards, there shouldn't be Ananasi, Corax, or Ratkin either. So my pleas, while logical, aren't supported by the canon. But I would argue those are mistakes in the setting. The developers allowed their gothic horror setting to become a fantasy setting, which was a mistake.<br /> <br /> Just my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, folklore is full of people turning into almost every animal imaginable. It's most often the effect of a curse, sorcery, or gods toying around, but that is something folklore of werewolves also shares. People turning into boars appear in norse and celtic folklore, because boars have symbolic significance there. I'm almost more surprised WW didn't go with a system to make a shapeshifter from a generic animal template for the Changing Breeds. This ironically makes the selection also seem arbitrary, so I don't disagree that some breeds are odd fits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-06T07:48:16-07:00","id":1536870,"title":"","content":"Fera that should seemingly be commonplace are absent to underline the tragedy of anthropogenic extinction and the overarching great extinction that humans bring with them (yes, it's done by Garou in the setting, but the Garou fucking up is just an allegory for humans fucking up). W:tA is really more of a &quot;did you know how terrible it really is outside?&quot; kind of horror over gothic horror, and the gothic sensibilities, via Vampire, are generally considered a thing that isn't good for the world, and therefore something that W:tA is going to struggle against in tone to its last word. This is why trying to &quot;reimagine&quot; W:tA to be more compatible with V:tM in WoD5 is particularly galling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-06T10:51:06-07:00","id":1536874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536769-why-the-hell-is-the-grondr-one-of-the-lost-breeds?p=1536861#post1536861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, is the world of Werewolf a Gothic Horror setting, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda depends how you want to define Gothic doesn't it?<br /> <br /> If, for example, one were to look at the rather copious notes compared to his contemporaries that Bram Stoker left on his world building for Dracula... Werewolf is pretty on point: a bunch of white people that read a bunch of books mostly written by other white people about things they didn't have first hand experience of, and then created a massive mish-mash of folklore from across multiple cultures, tossed in stuff just because it was cool, and then made a bunch of shit up on top of all of that to form something that at least feels cohesive. The Gothic authors were far more committed to mixing entertainment with societal critiques than they were about being faithful to folklore or mythology.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, that wasn't really unique to just the Gothic writers and the recognition of Gothic style as it's own thing stems from lots of other elements that separated them from other subgenres. So the argument that Werewolf isn't particularly Gothic usually comes from this angle instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-06T11:40:02-07:00","id":1536875,"title":"","content":"Bats and bears are hardly extinct either; the spiritual health of a species is linked to its existence as animals, but it's stated that the boars/pigs that wander the world now are more spiritually inert.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-06T15:42:20-07:00","id":1536878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536769-why-the-hell-is-the-grondr-one-of-the-lost-breeds?p=1536874#post1536874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kinda depends how you want to define Gothic doesn't it?<br /> <br /> If, for example, one were to look at the rather copious notes compared to his contemporaries that Bram Stoker left on his world building for Dracula... Werewolf is pretty on point: a bunch of white people that read a bunch of books mostly written by other white people about things they didn't have first hand experience of, and then created a massive mish-mash of folklore from across multiple cultures, tossed in stuff just because it was cool, and then made a bunch of shit up on top of all of that to form something that at least feels cohesive. The Gothic authors were far more committed to mixing entertainment with societal critiques than they were about being faithful to folklore or mythology.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, that wasn't really unique to just the Gothic writers and the recognition of Gothic style as it's own thing stems from lots of other elements that separated them from other subgenres. So the argument that Werewolf isn't particularly Gothic usually comes from this angle instead.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That is not a definition of Gothic genre I've seen before, nor does it apply to the specific tones of Gothic literture. It's amazing how on point it is, though. I would put the efforts of the latter writers in a more positive light, even if some times they really went hard into bad stereotypes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-10T03:21:55-07:00","id":1537141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536769-why-the-hell-is-the-grondr-one-of-the-lost-breeds?p=1536833#post1536833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Changing Breeds should reflect the actual real world legends of what animals that people turn into. And these tend to be actual predator animals. I don't think there are actual folklore or legends of people turning into Boars. So wereboars should not be thing in a Gothic horror world. That's more of a fantasy thing. The lost Breeds of Grondr, Apis, and Cazamotz make sense as breeds that don't survive as we do not have legends of them.<br /> <br /> I do realize that canon does have examples of such creatures. By folklore or mythological standards, there shouldn't be Ananasi, Corax, or Ratkin either. So my pleas, while logical, aren't supported by the canon. But I would argue those are mistakes in the setting. The developers allowed their gothic horror setting to become a fantasy setting, which was a mistake.<br /> <br /> Just my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div> I\u2019ve always felt that WEREWOLF being a setting that defaults to Horror, but can turn into Heroic Fantasy on a very, very good day for Our Heroes (Though never for very long) is part of it\u2019s charm: after all, if one wanted to play straight Gothic Horror we\u2019d be rolling up character for MASQUE OF THE READ DEATH instead!\ud83d\ude09<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T05:20:50-07:00","id":1537691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536769-why-the-hell-is-the-grondr-one-of-the-lost-breeds?p=1536861#post1536861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, is the world of Werewolf a Gothic Horror setting, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>I recently took a quick re-read of Ratkin book and it screams Splatterpunk all over XD (I really wish to have players for a ratkin chronicle now)<br /> <br /> Some people love it, some people hate it.<br /> But it goes for anything.<br /> <br /> I always felt like Werewolf is sort of Heroic Horror.<br /> It tickles the idea of being a monster, but it's more like 'I am a society pariah that still wants to do good despite everyone hating you because you're a monster&quot;.<br /> So I feel it tends to be more akin to a darker, edgier version of X-men for themes and mood instead of gothic narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T14:00:18-07:00","id":1539049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536769-why-the-hell-is-the-grondr-one-of-the-lost-breeds?p=1536833#post1536833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Changing Breeds should reflect the actual real world legends of what animals that people turn into.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my main problem with the changing breeds (and with a fair bit of werewolf lore [and with oWoD over CofD in general]) is how certain and hard a lot of things are. Ratfolk are Rat shifters and not Rat pooka or rodent-like Sluagh nor rat faced Gorgons or Fomor that happen to be able to breed true. Meanwhile despite the many myths surrounding shapechanging pinnipeds or porpoises, unless you count storytellers vault lost breeds or changeling breeds, they don't exist. And while the system allows for a lot of strange one of critters or lineages to exist, the lore rarely accommodates it instead defining things as relatively concrete groups with known or knowable tenants and objectives. There should be boar shifters, in the places where legends of talking boar-kings and wildmen who wear boar skins are told. I would want a line of were-dolphins that perhaps once ranged across the atlantic but are now reduced to a single lineage in the rivers of Brazil. I'd even take it as a Wyld spirit or the like who periodically posesses someone who lives along the rivers perhaps as an echo of a changing breed that was wiped out in the past, comparable to a mage avatar or changeling spirit. I think the setting, in every splat I've played, benefits from the degree of uncertainty that even the wisest mentor the PCs have access to might not know the true nature of the things that go bump in the night, or at least may not be willing or able to accurately communicate such things if they do know.<br /> <br /> I love the idea that theurges can ask the stones of a path to help them track someone but only be told about the strength of footfalls, that inhuman sources have inhuman perceptions and priorities that would make it difficult for them to give you the answers important to you, even if they wanted to. I love the idea that large parts of the Silver Record have been lost forever, destroyed in wars or by foes or even by erstwhile Gaian Garou who wanted some things to be forgotten and so obliterated entire epics and fables.<br /> <br /> For that matter, to disagree with OP, it also makes sense that some of the strange and wild things of the world are gone, lost forever or indelibly corrupted. Like the idea of 'our ancestors wiped this out and it never returned' adds a delightful bittersweet note to Garou trying to act as protectors of Gaia and fight against forces of extinction. And it makes sense that if you kill all of a particular flower, no matter how plentiful your garden, it would take a miracle to see that flower bloom again. So, despite the abundant wild kinfolk of the Grondr, it would take a miracle for a new and uncorrupted line of Grondr to emerge from the ruin heaped on their line. It'd be comparable to the singular White Howler being born from a modern Welsh family except without a Nation looking out for her to try and tell her what to be or not to be. And if traditional genocide proved tedious even for the warriors of Gaia, less traditional methods, such as killing or corrupting the Boar-shifters patron spirits, severing their connection to luna or Helios or whichever incarna chooses them, or the like, are possibilities.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, if you really want Grondr to be out there, in the sunlit realm, with human and wild boar kinfolk, <b>maybe</b>, a bit like the Ananasi or the Naga, they have made some kind of powerful spirit pact that makes it difficult for Garou to perceive or track them. A kind of Arcane background but just for Garou, or maybe shifters as a whole, and the Garou are too arrogant and stretched too thin in modern nights to see through it. Or <b>maybe </b>part of the genocide was that Grondr had some creation rites to prevent them from being too populous similar to corax, or opposite of ratkin, which the Garou disrupted as part of the genocide and and non-skull-pig heritors now use sparingly and in secret, a la the Salubri of VtM, intentionally keeping their number small and well trained to avoid their ancestral adversaries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27296-devidramoth","name":"Devidramoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27296_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T06:47:46-07:00","id":1539203,"title":"","content":"A few things, that I'd have to check. What percentage of wild pig populations DON'T have domesticated or feral stock mixed in? Dogs and most wolf-dog hybrids can not become Garou. Thus it's worth speculating if that was the case.<br /> <br /> In more concrete lore terms the remaining Grondr got filled with too much hatred that they cast aside their purpose and became the Skull Pigs in an attempt to get revenge. They are now a twisted version of themselves who must eat Wyrm taint to gain intelligence and gifts (or to known themselves). Which could provide an interesting story hook for Garou if the only remaining Garou were to become BSDs what would their version of the Skull Pig look like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28181-a-bunch-of-gamers","name":"A Bunch of Gamers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28181_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}